@@ -2,6 +2,25 @@
 
 Deployment helpers for the internal services.
 
-`bin/notify-deploy.sh SERVICE VERSION` restarts the service on the deploy host and posts a
-message to the release channel. The webhook URL comes from `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` in the
-environment; per-service settings live in `etc/services.conf`.
+`bin/notify-deploy.sh [--dry-run] SERVICE VERSION [NOTE]` restarts the service on the deploy
+host and posts a message to the release channel. The webhook URL comes from
+`SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL` in the environment; per-service settings live in `etc/services.conf`.
+
+- `SERVICE` must match `[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*` and `VERSION` must start with a letter or digit and
+  contain only letters, digits, `.`, `_`, `+` and `-` (64 characters at most each).
+- `NOTE` is an optional short release note (500 characters at most). When given, it appears in
+  the Slack message on a second line, after `Release note:`. Quote it so it is one argument:
+
+  ```
+  bin/notify-deploy.sh web 1.4.2 "Fixes the login timeout"
+  ```
+
+- `--dry-run` prints the remote command and the Slack payload that would be used, then exits
+  without restarting the service or posting. It needs no `SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL`, and the URL is
+  never printed.
+
+  ```
+  bin/notify-deploy.sh --dry-run web 1.4.2 "Fixes the login timeout"
+  ```
+
+`jq` must be installed.
